WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:15.140
lunch the earl summoned Cedric to the library.

2
00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.501
"Thank you for the toys!"

3
00:00:19.061 --> 00:00:21.221
Cedric cried as he raced into the room.

4
00:00:21.241 --> 00:00:26.203
"There's one that's like baseball, only you play it on a board with pegs.

5
00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:28.923
I tried to explain it to Mrs.

6
00:00:28.983 --> 00:00:31.124
Mellon, but she didn't understand the game.

7
00:00:32.296 --> 00:00:34.457
You know all about baseball, right?"

8
00:00:34.477 --> 00:00:39.059
"I'm afraid I don't," the earl said.

9
00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:42.221
"It's an American sport."

10
00:00:44.061 --> 00:00:45.842
"Would you like me to show you my game?

11
00:00:47.143 --> 00:00:49.644
Or does your foot hurt too much right now?"

12
00:00:49.664 --> 00:00:55.106
"Go and get the game," the earl said.

13
00:00:56.047 --> 00:00:58.588
Once again the earl noticed Cedric's thoughtfulness.

14
00:01:01.332 --> 00:01:03.533
He almost smiled when Cedric returned.

15
00:01:03.553 --> 00:01:07.136
"May I pull that table over to your chair?"

16
00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:08.476
Cedric asked.

17
00:01:08.496 --> 00:01:13.980
"Ring for the footman, and he'll move it for you," the earl said.

18
00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.441
"I can do it myself.

19
00:01:16.521 --> 00:01:17.522
It's not too heavy."

20
00:01:19.743 --> 00:01:23.705
The earl watched with amusement as Cedric dragged the table into place.

21
00:01:25.066 --> 00:01:28.088
Then he took the game from the box and arranged it on the table.

22
00:01:29.276 --> 00:01:31.998
Cedric explained how each peg represented a player.

23
00:01:33.338 --> 00:01:36.540
Finally he summarized the rules of baseball for the earl.

24
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:41.643
"And that's how you score a run," Cedric said.

25
00:01:41.663 --> 00:01:43.304
"Let's play!"

26
00:01:47.186 --> 00:01:51.388
Cedric and his grandfather were absorbed in the game when a footman announced a visitor.

27
00:01:53.569 --> 00:01:57.932
Reverend Mordaunt, minister of the village church, had arrived full of dread.

28
00:01:59.028 --> 00:02:02.891
He'd heard that the earl's gout was bad and that Cedric had arrived.

29
00:02:03.952 --> 00:02:06.914
He was sure the earl would be in a worse mood than usual.

30
00:02:08.735 --> 00:02:11.998
So he was surprised to find the earl having fun with Cedric.

31
00:02:12.018 --> 00:02:16.421
"They seem to be getting along," Reverend Mordaunt thought.

32
00:02:16.441 --> 00:02:21.785
"But I'm sure his mood will change when he learns why I'm here.

33
00:02:22.645 --> 00:02:25.768
He always thinks his tenants are to blame when they need help."

34
00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:32.222
"Be careful," Cedric said to his grandfather.

35
00:02:32.242 --> 00:02:35.184
"One more out, and I win."

36
00:02:35.204 --> 00:02:39.026
"The game's not over yet."

37
00:02:40.347 --> 00:02:43.628
The earl realized the minister was waiting to be greeted.

38
00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:48.531
"Good afternoon, Reverend Mordaunt.

39
00:02:49.592 --> 00:02:52.874
As you can see, I'm trying something different."

40
00:02:54.415 --> 00:02:56.676
The earl laid his hand on Cedric's shoulder.

41
00:02:57.644 --> 00:03:00.105
"This is the new Lord Fauntleroy.

42
00:03:02.746 --> 00:03:05.407
Cedric, this is Reverend Mordaunt."

43
00:03:09.429 --> 00:03:13.491
Cedric shook hands with the minister and then leaned against his grandfather's chair.

44
00:03:13.511 --> 00:03:15.392
"Take a seat, reverend."

45
00:03:18.033 --> 00:03:21.174
The usual stern look had returned to the earl's face.

46
00:03:21.194 --> 00:03:23.435
"Why are you here?

47
00:03:24.035 --> 00:03:25.276
Who's in trouble now?"

48
00:03:27.108 --> 00:03:32.172
"One of your tenant farmers has been sick for a long time," the minister began.

49
00:03:32.192 --> 00:03:36.394
"Now he's behind on the rent and about to be evicted.

50
00:03:37.575 --> 00:03:39.396
His wife begged me to talk to you.

51
00:03:40.497 --> 00:03:43.019
If they have to leave, they'll starve.

52
00:03:43.659 --> 00:03:48.042
He's a good man—" "That sounds just like Mary and her husband!"

53
00:03:49.103 --> 00:03:51.304
Cedric looked eagerly at his grandfather.

54
00:03:51.324 --> 00:03:54.847
"Remember how I used your money to help them?"

55
00:03:54.867 --> 00:03:58.821
"So what would you do in this case?"

56
00:03:59.421 --> 00:04:00.441
the earl asked.

57
00:04:00.461 --> 00:04:06.043
"I'd give them time to catch up on the rent and send them some food."

58
00:04:06.063 --> 00:04:11.404
"You heard his lordship," the earl said to the minister.

59
00:04:11.424 --> 00:04:14.105
"Tell my tenant the good news.

60
00:04:15.205 --> 00:04:19.086
And on your way out, tell my cook to send them a basket of food every day."

61
00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:25.868
After Reverend Mordaunt left, Cedric asked to visit his mother.

62
00:04:27.348 --> 00:04:30.029
The earl wanted to cut that tie as soon as possible.

63
00:04:30.970 --> 00:04:32.770
"You can go another day.

64
00:04:33.951 --> 00:04:36.672
There's something for you to see in the stables now."

65
00:04:36.692 --> 00:04:41.034
"I'm sorry, but my mother is expecting me."

66
00:04:41.054 --> 00:04:45.296
"Don't you want to see your pony?"

67
00:04:46.716 --> 00:04:47.937
Cedric looked shocked.

68
00:04:47.957 --> 00:04:50.818
"My pony?

69
00:04:50.838 --> 00:04:54.500
Mine—like all the things upstairs?"

70
00:04:56.500 --> 00:05:00.021
The earl knew his grandson couldn't resist this temptation.

71
00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:03.562
"You can visit your mother tomorrow."

72
00:05:03.582 --> 00:05:08.783
"No, I can't," Cedric said firmly.

73
00:05:08.803 --> 00:05:13.105
"I've been missing Mama all morning, so I know she's missing me."

74
00:05:15.485 --> 00:05:17.946
The earl heaved an exasperated sigh.

75
00:05:17.966 --> 00:05:23.047
"Fine, you may visit your mother."

76
00:05:26.284 --> 00:05:29.325
Half an hour later, the two of them settled into the carriage.

77
00:05:29.345 --> 00:05:35.388
"I think you must be the best person in the world."

78
00:05:36.348 --> 00:05:38.429
Cedric turned toward his grandfather.

79
00:05:38.449 --> 00:05:42.371
"Me?" the earl said in surprise.

80
00:05:42.391 --> 00:05:45.832
"You help so many people.

81
00:05:47.373 --> 00:05:52.455
Mr. Hobbs thought earls were tyrants, but you're the kindest man I know.

82
00:05:53.736 --> 00:05:57.057
When I grow up, I want to be just like you."

83
00:05:57.077 --> 00:06:00.238
"Just like me."

84
00:06:01.599 --> 00:06:04.440
The earl turned away so he didn't have to face Cedric.

85
00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.522
He was deep in thought when they arrived at the cottage.

86
00:06:08.542 --> 00:06:15.104
"I'll help you out," Cedric said as the carriage door opened.

87
00:06:16.105 --> 00:06:17.305
The earl shook his head.

88
00:06:17.325 --> 00:06:19.986
"I'm not getting out."

89
00:06:21.407 --> 00:06:22.367
"Not getting out?"

90
00:06:22.828 --> 00:06:23.488
Cedric said.

91
00:06:24.484 --> 00:06:26.086
"My mother will be disappointed."

92
00:06:26.106 --> 00:06:32.433
"I'm not so sure about that," the earl muttered.

93
00:06:32.453 --> 00:06:37.218
"Tell her not even a new pony could keep you away."

94
00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:42.064
The earl watched Cedric run up the drive and into his mother's arms.
